outfit `Z-3600 "Beam" Amat Torch`
	plural `Z-3600 "Beam" Amat Torches`
	category "Engines"
	series "Engines"
	index 07080
	"cost" 300000000
	thumbnail "outfit/beam antimatter drive"
	"mass" 3600
	"outfit space" -360
	"engine capacity" -360
	"thrust" 600
	"thrusting energy" 15
	"thrusting heat" 90
	"thrusting fuel" 0.3
	"drag reduction" 9
	"flare sprite" "effect/avgi flare/antimatter"
		"frame rate" 15
	"flare sound" "fusion torch"
	"turn" 6000
	"turning energy" 9
	"turning heat" 54
	"steering flare sprite" "effect/avgi flare/rcs"
		"frame rate" 15
		"scale" 0.5
	"steering flare sound" "remnant afterburner"
	"magnetic nozzle" 18
	description "The fastest Avgi starships were propelled not just by their engines, but also by immense banks of lasers and particle beams stationed in the Anax system, pushing ships to velocities in excess of 0.2c before braking with a magsail or plasma magnet. Just before the invention of the hyperdrive, however, the Avgi perfected this beam-core antimatter drive, capable of pushing a starship with sufficient antimatter fuel to 0.4c and perhaps beyond. Requiring immense quantities of antimatter, the amat farms around Anax such as Antivli Station would have been strained to their limits had this design entered mass production, but the surprise invention of the hyperdrive rendered it laughably obsolete overnight."

outfit "Teciimach Canister"
	category "Ammunition"
	series "Ammunition"
	index 03020
	cost 35500
	thumbnail "outfit/emp torpedo"
	"mass" 1
	"teciimach canister capacity" -1
	description "This canister contains everything required to assemble a Teciimach Torpedo. These weapons emit strong electromagnetic pulses which interfere with a ship's generators and neutralize a portion of their energy."
	description `	Unlike the previous generation of "EMP Torpedoes," the Teciimach torpedoes actively shape their emission pattern to avoid impacting their allies.`

outfit "Teciimach Canister Rack"
	category "Ammunition"
	series "Ammunition"
	index 03021
	licenses
		Remnant
	cost 295000
	thumbnail "outfit/emp rack"
	"mass" 5
	"outfit space" -9
	"energy capacity" 500
	"teciimach canister capacity" 9
	ammo "Teciimach Canister"
	description "The Teciimach Canister Rack is used to store extra sets of components, both to expand the capacity of a ship, and on carriers for resupplying fighters."
	description "	In addition to its ammunition capacity, the storage bay can also contain a small amount of charge, enough to let an otherwise battery-less ship assemble Teciimach Torpedoes."
